= Topic portal =

Reusable navigation shell for portals and subportals that should not be forced to correspond one-to-one with a semantic Domain.

<pre>
{{Topic portal
 |title=Python
 |parent=[[Portal:Computer science|Computer science]]
 |category=Python
 |description=Focused entry point...
 |start=Begin with syntax and data...
 |learning_path='''Foundations''' → '''Core''' → '''Technical'''
 |subportals=
 |tree=<categorytree mode="pages" depth="2">Python</categorytree>
 |related=[[Portal:Computer science|Computer science]]
}}
</pre>

Use <code>parent</code> to expose a navigational breadcrumb and <code>subportals</code> to make recursive portal structures explicit. Neither field asserts ontology inheritance.

[[Category:BITwiki templates]]
